<VI _name="RemoteVI Complex Fixture.vi" description="Event-logging test fixture of the RemoteVI integration tests for a complex application UI (tests\5Clv\5Ccomplex.test.mjs). Its panel is NI's Resizable Panel with Splitter Bars example with three panes (left\2C toolbar\2C main) and an unlocked vertical and horizontal splitter bar\3B RemoteVI Complex Fixture Arrange.vi lays it out. Left pane\3A tree Nav\2C table Results\2C array of clusters Steps (the pane scrolls). Toolbar\3A Inspector\2C ring View\2C Stop\2C string Status. Main pane (its tab control scales with the pane)\3A tab control Settings with the page Acquisition (cluster Channel with Name\2C Gain and Enabled\2C slide Rate\2C knob Level\2C path Data File with browse button) and the page Display (graph Scope with cursors)\2C and the subpanel Viewer\2C which shows RemoteVI Complex View A.vi or View B.vi\2C both running\2C swapped by View. Inspector opens RemoteVI Complex Inspector.vi as a separate\2C non-modal window (FP.Open\2C Run VI). At start it truncates or creates the log (Log Path\2C or RemoteVI Complex Fixture.log in the system temp directory)\2C writes layout lines (panel coordinates of every control in every pane\2C tab page and cluster) and pane lines\2C publishes its panel on port 8089 and writes ready. RemoteVI Complex Fixture Events.vi handles the events (all registered dynamically\2C so the panel can come from another VI) and sends its lines\2C like the views and the inspector\2C through the named queue RemoteVI Complex Fixture\3B the housekeeping loop here writes them to the log every 100 ms\2C shows the last in Status and writes the layout and pane lines again whenever they changed (a splitter was dragged\2C a pane scrolled). Stop sends the named notifier RemoteVI Complex Fixture\2C which ends the event loop\2C the housekeeping loop\2C the views and the inspector.">
